  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. It focuses on small-probability outcomes (less than 20%) and adjusts their weights upward by 10 percentage points. In Lottery A, both outcomes have a 50% probability, which is not below 20%, so no weighting adjustment applies. In Lottery B, the 500 Euro outcome has a 100% probability, also not below 20%. Therefore, no outcome in either lottery qualifies for the probability weighting adjustment specified in the reason. As a result, the adjusted weighted sums of outcomes remain identical to the unweighted expected values: 500 Euro for Lottery A (0.5 × 1000 + 0.5 × 0) and 500 Euro for Lottery B (1.0 × 500). The decision reason would thus be indifferent between the two lotteries, since no outcome falls below the 20% threshold and no reweighting occurs.",
